 between the 90 s failover and the 240 s pager. Plausibility is not\n  the sign-off the plan required, though, and this constant decides how long a worker slot is held per stalled call.\n\nAll five passes agree with this finding. It was carried over from the previous review and re-confirmed.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Get an explicit operator answer: budget-30, budget-120 or budget-300.\n- If the answer is not 120, change only the constant.\n\n### WR-02: Verification, validation and summary docs say the human gate is unnecessary or was met\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:4,73-75,84`; also `01-VALIDATION.md:51-53,59` and\n`01-01-SUMMARY.md:94-96`\n\n**Issue:** Four statements contradict WR-01, which is still open in `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md`:\n\n| Where | What it says |\n|-------|--------------|\n| VERIFICATION frontmatter | `status: passed` |\n| VERIFICATION, \"Human Verification Required\" | \"None\", reasoning from the plan's own figures in place of the required human answer |\n| VERIFICATION, line 84 | calls WR-01 \"non-blocking\" |\n| VALIDATION | \"All phase behaviors have automated verification\" and \"All tasks have `<automated>` verify\". Task 1 has no `<verify>` block, and D2 has no automated verification. |\n| SUMMARY | \"Deviations from Plan: None\", although a blocking-human gate was answered without a human |\n\nProposed Critical by the doc-accuracy pass; see the Summary for why it is classified Warning here.\n\n**Fix:**\n- In VERIFICATION, list D2 (confirm the 120 s value) under Human Verification Required, set `status: human_needed`,\n  and drop \"non-blocking\" from line 84.\n- In VALIDATION, add D2 as a manual-only verification.\n- In the SUMMARY, record the gate deviation.\n\nRe-run `/gsd-verify-work 1` rather than hand-editing where a GSD command owns the file.\n\n### WR-03: Completion and \"shipped\" state is claimed before ship and before sign-off\n\n**File:** `.planning/PROJECT.md:13-15,25`; `.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md:5,12`; `.planning/STATE.md:4-5,22`;\nuntracked `.planning/state.json`\n\n**Issue:** These docs state completion that has not happened:\n\n| Where | What it says |\n|-------|--------------|\n| PROJECT.md | \"Shipped in Phase 1\", and BUDGET-01 under \"Validated\" |\n| REQUIREMENTS.md | BUDGET-01 is `[x]` and `Complete` |\n| STATE.md | `status: completed`, \"all phases complete\" |\n| `.planning/state.json` (untracked) | `\"phases\": []`, routing to `/gsd-new-milestone` because \"All phases complete\" |\n\nWhat is actually true at review time:\n- `feature/phase-01` has no upstream.\n- `gh pr list --state all` returns `[]`.\n- `origin/main` is still `f976b94`.\n- WR-01 is open.\n\nAutomation that reads `state.json` would skip shipping and start a new milestone.\n\n**Fix:**\n- PROJECT.md: change \"Shipped\" to \"Implemented on feature/phase-01, pending operator confirmation and merge\".\n- Keep BUDGET-01 as implemented but awaiting sign-off until WR-01 is answered.\n- Do not commit `state.json` in its current form.\n\n### WR-04: The repository has no CI, so the PR will show zero checks\n\n**File:** repository root (no `.github/workflows/`, no pyproject/tox/Makefile on HEAD, `main` or `integration`)\n\n**Issue:**\n- `gh api repos/denniyahh/p50-live-attempt-2/actions/workflows` returns `total_count: 0`.\n- Branch protection returns HTTP 403 on this plan, so no check can be required.\n- The only \"tests pass\" evidence is local agent runs recorded in the SUMMARY and VERIFICATION.\n- A PR with zero checks looks green by absence.\n\n**Fix:** Add `.github/workflows/test.yml` that runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t . -v` on push and on\npull_request. Gate merge on `gh pr checks <PR>` for the head SHA.\n\n### WR-05: The test cannot tell the three offered budgets apart\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget.py:5,11` (backs `probe/budget.py:1`)\n\n**Issue:**\n- Scratch-copy mutation runs: budget 30 gives exit 0, 120 gives 0, 300 gives 0, and 45 gives exit 1.\n- The plan itself 