 returns `start_secs + budget`. Probes:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|-------|--------|\n| `10` | `130` (an int, despite `-> float`) |\n| `True` | `121` |\n| `nan` | `nan` |\n| `inf` | `inf` |\n| `\"x\"` or `None` | `TypeError` |\n\n**Fix:** None required. If callers might pass a bad clock value, optionally reject non-finite input with\n`math.isfinite`.\n\n## What this review does not establish\n\n- **The 90 s / 240 s figures:** they were taken from the plan text and not checked against the real upstream or pager\n  configuration.\n- **Type checking:** no static type checker ran, because mypy and pyright are not installed.\n- **Mutation testing:** mutants were written by hand, not by a mutation tool, so other mutants may survive.\n- **Python version:** only Python 3.15.0 was used.\n- **Secret scanning:** gitleaks used its default rules, so a custom-format or low-entropy secret could slip past it.\n  Only `main..HEAD` and the working tree were scanned.\n- **Remote state:** it reflects `git ls-remote` and `gh` at review time.\n\n---\n\n_Reviewed: 2026-10-21_\n_Reviewer: Claude (multi-angle: doc-accuracy, security, CI/build, external-state, generalist; merged by orchestrator)_\n_Depth: deep_\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":62,"newStart":1,"newLines":324,"lines":[" ---"," phase: 01-retry-budget","-reviewed: 2026-10-21T00:00:00Z","-depth: standard","-files_reviewed: 2","+reviewed: 2026-10-21T21:05:00Z","+depth: deep","+files_reviewed: 4"," files_reviewed_list:","+  - devflow.toml","   - probe/__init__.py","   - probe/budget.py","+  - tests/test_budget.py"," findings:","   critical: 0","-  warning: 1","-  info: 3","-  total: 4","+  warning: 7","+  info: 8","+  total: 15"," status: issues_found"," ---"," "," # Phase 01: Code Review Report"," "," **Reviewed:** 2026-10-21","-**Depth:** standard","-**Files Reviewed:** 2","+**Depth:** deep (multi-angle)","+**Files Reviewed:** 4 source/config files, plus every `.planning/` doc in `git diff main..HEAD` cross-referenced 